<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="5" dur="4.5">services, Mr. Trevor Reagan.</text><text start="20.305" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="22.7" dur="2.7">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Good afternoon.</text><text start="25.8" dur="3.4">I&amp;#39;m Trevor Reagan, and I lead</text><text start="27.6" dur="3.6">humanitarian services for the American</text><text start="29.2" dur="3.7">Red Cross. But before I get started</text><text start="31.2" dur="3.6">today, I want to say a special thank you</text><text start="32.9" dur="3.2">to First Lady Melania Trump</text><text start="34.8" dur="3.6">and Second Lady Usha Vance for their</text><text start="36.1" dur="4.3">presence here today. Being here creates</text><text start="38.4" dur="2.9">so much attention on our service members</text><text start="40.4" dur="2.4">and their families that are so</text><text start="41.3" dur="4.1">desperately needed.</text><text start="42.8" dur="4.9">And also to our base and wing commanders</text><text start="45.4" dur="4">at Joint Joint Base Andrews,</text><text start="47.7" dur="4">we thank you for your presence and for</text><text start="49.4" dur="4.4">your leadership.</text><text start="51.7" dur="4.6">For more than 145 years, the American</text><text start="53.8" dur="3.6">Red Cross has stood beside the military</text><text start="56.3" dur="3.8">community.</text><text start="57.4" dur="5.4">But today really isn&amp;#39;t about history.</text><text start="60.1" dur="4.3">Today is about people, people who serve,</text><text start="62.8" dur="3.5">people who wait at home,</text><text start="64.4" dur="3.5">and people who step forward when help is</text><text start="66.3" dur="3.9">needed.</text><text start="67.9" dur="3.6">For our service members here today,</text><text start="70.2" dur="3.5">we know some of you may not get home for</text><text start="71.5" dur="4.3">the holidays. Some are just coming off a</text><text start="73.7" dur="4.3">deployment, some heading to deployment,</text><text start="75.8" dur="4.4">and many are balancing the pressures of</text><text start="78" dur="3.6">family life with military service</text><text start="80.2" dur="3.2">in a way most of us will never</text><text start="81.6" dur="6">understand.</text><text start="83.4" dur="4.2">We see you and we are grateful.</text><text start="87.9" dur="4.5">Now today, this special event we&amp;#39;re here</text><text start="90.3" dur="4.2">to do together, in a few moments we&amp;#39;ll</text><text start="92.4" dur="4.4">start putting together comfort kits and</text><text start="94.5" dur="4.7">sign holiday cards, and really it&amp;#39;s all</text><text start="96.8" dur="3.9">about one very simple message.</text><text start="99.2" dur="3.1">To those troops overseas, these cards</text><text start="100.7" dur="3.7">will go to</text><text start="102.3" dur="4.8">you&amp;#39;re not alone, and we are thinking of</text><text start="104.4" dur="4">you throughout this holiday season.</text><text start="107.1" dur="3.1">Now in my time with the Red Cross, I&amp;#39;ve</text><text start="108.4" dur="3.4">realized that service is not just an</text><text start="110.2" dur="3.8">individual commitment,</text><text start="111.8" dur="3.3">it&amp;#39;s also a family commitment.</text><text start="114" dur="2.2">And as the wife of a Marine Corps</text><text start="115.1" dur="3.3">veteran,</text><text start="116.2" dur="4.692">Mrs. Vance understands the personal</text><text start="118.4" dur="4.292">connections in that tradition, but also</text><text start="120.892" dur="3.7">appreciates the service of our military</text><text start="122.692" dur="3.2">members and the sacrifice</text><text start="124.592" dur="2.6">that their family makes every single</text><text start="125.892" dur="3.2">day.</text><text start="127.192" dur="5.9">So please join me in welcoming our</text><text start="129.092" dur="4">nation&amp;#39;s second lady, Usha Vance.</text><text start="136.896" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="142.136" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="146.721" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="150.192" dur="3.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Hello everyone. It&amp;#39;s my pleasure to be</text><text start="152.392" dur="2.9">here with you today.</text><text start="153.992" dur="3.3">I&amp;#39;m so delighted that we have the</text><text start="155.292" dur="3.9">opportunity to reconvene this holiday</text><text start="157.292" dur="4">season and give back to our men and</text><text start="159.192" dur="4.6">women in uniform.</text><text start="161.292" dur="4">I want to start by thanking Trevor Regan</text><text start="163.792" dur="3.8">and the rest of the team at the American</text><text start="165.292" dur="5">Red Cross for all their work in keeping</text><text start="167.592" dur="4.3">our nation healthy and safe.</text><text start="170.292" dur="3.5">And I&amp;#39;d like to offer my gratitude</text><text start="171.892" dur="5.3">specifically to the Americans serving</text><text start="173.792" dur="5.4">right here at Joint Base Andrews.</text><text start="177.192" dur="4.2">Over the last two years, JD and I have</text><text start="179.192" dur="4.4">come to know the base very well.</text><text start="181.392" dur="4.4">And I can&amp;#39;t overstate how incredibly</text><text start="183.592" dur="4.4">kind and helpful everyone stationed here</text><text start="185.792" dur="4.1">has been to our family, as well as to</text><text start="187.992" dur="4">all the staff members and guests who</text><text start="189.892" dur="3.7">pass through its gates.</text><text start="191.992" dur="3.6">We always look forward to our visits to</text><text start="193.592" dur="4.2">America&amp;#39;s airfield, and today is no</text><text start="195.592" dur="3.6">exception.</text><text start="197.792" dur="2.7">And with just three days until</text><text start="199.192" dur="2.8">Thanksgiving,</text><text start="200.492" dur="3.4">the first lady and I are particularly</text><text start="201.992" dur="4.2">grateful to be here and to take part in</text><text start="203.892" dur="4">a tradition that dates back well over a</text><text start="206.192" dur="3.3">century.</text><text start="207.892" dur="3.2">This morning, we&amp;#39;re joining with</text><text start="209.492" dur="3.5">military spouses from the base to</text><text start="211.092" dur="4.1">assemble care packages for members of</text><text start="212.992" dur="5.4">our armed forces currently serving</text><text start="215.192" dur="5.1">deployments away from their loved ones.</text><text start="218.392" dur="3.5">Each year, the Red Cross spearheads this</text><text start="220.292" dur="3.8">effort.</text><text start="221.892" dur="4">It&amp;#39;s a simple, elegant way of expressing</text><text start="224.092" dur="3.8">gratitude to the Americans who put their</text><text start="225.892" dur="3.9">nation before themselves</text><text start="227.892" dur="3.5">and reminding them that even when</text><text start="229.792" dur="4.7">they&amp;#39;re far from home,</text><text start="231.392" dur="4.5">their country has not forgotten them.</text><text start="234.492" dur="3.2">I hope these packages serve as a</text><text start="235.892" dur="4.9">reminder that their sacrifices are</text><text start="237.692" dur="4.902">deeply appreciated and that their nation</text><text start="240.792" dur="3.902">and our family looks forward to them</text><text start="242.594" dur="4">back home.</text><text start="244.694" dur="4">But before I step away,</text><text start="246.594" dur="3.7">I&amp;#39;d like to thank someone who is deeply</text><text start="248.694" dur="4.5">committed to the well-being of our</text><text start="250.294" dur="4.8">service members and their loved ones.</text><text start="253.194" dur="4">Our First Lady has made supporting</text><text start="255.094" dur="4.1">America&amp;#39;s children and families,</text><text start="257.194" dur="4.4">including and especially those who serve</text><text start="259.194" dur="4.4">in our military, a central part of her</text><text start="261.594" dur="3.9">leadership.</text><text start="263.594" dur="4.2">It&amp;#39;s a great privilege to join her in</text><text start="265.494" dur="4.2">this tradition once again. So, ladies</text><text start="267.794" dur="3.5">and gentlemen, please join me in</text><text start="269.694" dur="5.2">welcoming the First Lady of the United</text><text start="271.294" dur="3.6">States, Melania Trump.</text><text start="275.103" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [music]</text><text start="284.273" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="290.168" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="297.373" dur="2.02">[music]</text><text start="301.594" dur="4.7">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Good afternoon.</text><text start="303.394" dur="5.8">Thank you, Usha, for your kind words and</text><text start="306.294" dur="4.9">for the dedication and service that you</text><text start="309.194" dur="4.9">and the Vice President,</text><text start="311.194" dur="6.5">a proud United States Marine veteran,</text><text start="314.094" dur="6.8">have provided to our nation.</text><text start="317.694" dur="5.7">It is an honor to be welcomed by all of</text><text start="320.894" dur="4.9">the members of our armed forces and</text><text start="323.394" dur="5.5">their beautiful families here</text><text start="325.794" dur="5.2">at Joint Base Andrews.</text><text start="328.894" dur="4.6">I&amp;#39;m delighted to share this special</text><text start="330.994" dur="5.8">afternoon with you.</text><text start="333.494" dur="6.6">And thank you to the spouses of our</text><text start="336.794" dur="7.4">cabinet members who have joined me today</text><text start="340.094" dur="4.1">to support America&amp;#39;s military.</text><text start="344.394" dur="8.3">Perfect precision is not an accident.</text><text start="349.194" dur="4.7">It is the result of repetition, measured</text><text start="352.694" dur="4.2">pacing,</text><text start="353.894" dur="5.6">and flawless execution.</text><text start="356.894" dur="4.9">The US military is the most powerful</text><text start="359.494" dur="3.9">military in the world because of its</text><text start="361.794" dur="4.801">people.</text><text start="363.394" dur="5.901">Our warriors train</text><text start="366.595" dur="5.2">pushing the boundaries of physical and</text><text start="369.295" dur="5.8">mental strength.</text><text start="371.795" dur="5.5">Every moment is deliberate. Everything</text><text start="375.095" dur="4.5">is designed to achieve overpowering</text><text start="377.295" dur="4.8">military superiority</text><text start="379.595" dur="5.6">through relentless training, technical</text><text start="382.095" dur="6.3">mastery, and a very measured approach to</text><text start="385.195" dur="7.5">everything they do. Our warriors make</text><text start="388.395" dur="7.4">the very complex look effortless.</text><text start="392.695" dur="5">But I know our military is not a</text><text start="395.795" dur="4.1">machine.</text><text start="397.695" dur="5.2">It&amp;#39;s made up of human</text><text start="399.895" dur="5.8">beings, sons and daughters</text><text start="402.895" dur="4.2">who are taking on this inherently big</text><text start="405.695" dur="4.3">risk.</text><text start="407.095" dur="5.9">Our brave men and women have families</text><text start="409.995" dur="4.4">who are praying for their safety every</text><text start="412.995" dur="3.8">day.</text><text start="414.395" dur="3.7">Those families know that absolute</text><text start="416.795" dur="4.3">precision</text><text start="418.095" dur="5.2">and coordination are vital to protecting</text><text start="421.095" dur="6.5">the people they love.</text><text start="423.295" dur="7.4">There is no room for mistakes.</text><text start="427.595" dur="5.7">Our warriors are united by a vision</text><text start="430.695" dur="5.7">greater than themselves.</text><text start="433.295" dur="6.8">Each individual contributes to a larger</text><text start="436.395" dur="6.2">plan with their fellow warriors.</text><text start="440.095" dur="4.2">They have unwavering trust in each</text><text start="442.595" dur="6.7">other.</text><text start="444.295" dur="7.5">There cannot be any accidents.</text><text start="449.295" dur="4.7">We must always remember that their</text><text start="451.795" dur="5.4">service is not just about the</text><text start="453.995" dur="5.5">transaction of a single mission.</text><text start="457.195" dur="4">It is about the future of our children</text><text start="459.495" dur="4.1">and grandchildren.</text><text start="461.195" dur="3.7">It is about maintaining America&amp;#39;s lead</text><text start="463.595" dur="4.3">position</text><text start="464.895" dur="6.4">in the world, creating opportunities for</text><text start="467.895" dur="6.9">American ingenuity and innovation,</text><text start="471.295" dur="6.2">and preserving the safety and freedom of</text><text start="474.795" dur="5.1">future generations.</text><text start="477.495" dur="3.7">Our leaders do not always talk about</text><text start="479.895" dur="4.1">this,</text><text start="481.195" dur="8.002">but we must always remember this is the</text><text start="483.995" dur="5.202">end result of our military action.</text><text start="489.597" dur="6.2">The American Red Cross assists member of</text><text start="492.997" dur="5.5">the military and their families.</text><text start="495.797" dur="4.7">And for this I&amp;#39;m grateful.</text><text start="498.497" dur="4.8">They serve troops and their families</text><text start="500.497" dur="4.8">worldwide. And today&amp;#39;s tradition will</text><text start="503.297" dur="4.4">deliver packages filled with warm</text><text start="505.297" dur="5">holiday season wishes</text><text start="507.697" dur="5">made with love which will be well</text><text start="510.297" dur="5.7">received.</text><text start="512.697" dur="5">The strength of our military helps us</text><text start="515.997" dur="4.3">prevent wars.</text><text start="517.697" dur="5.9">We perfect our capabilities</text><text start="520.297" dur="6.6">to protect human life, preserve peace,</text><text start="523.597" dur="5.7">and secure our nation&amp;#39;s future.</text><text start="526.897" dur="5.3">This high level of precision</text><text start="529.297" dur="5.8">of our armed forces sends an</text><text start="532.197" dur="4.2">unmistakable message to the rest of the</text><text start="535.097" dur="6.8">world.</text><text start="536.397" dur="5.5">America&amp;#39;s children must inherit peace.</text><text start="542.197" dur="3.9">I wish America a very happy</text><text start="544.497" dur="4.7">Thanksgiving,</text><text start="546.097" dur="4.7">safety and peace during this upcoming</text><text start="549.197" dur="3.629">holiday season.</text><text start="550.797" dur="4.049">Thank you.</text><text start="552.826" dur="2.02">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; [applause]</text><text start="730.699" dur="2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I</text><text start="863.701" dur="2.1">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Hello.</text><text start="1108.903" dur="2.1">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; It</text><text start="1230.905" dur="2.1">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I</text><text start="1476.707" dur="2.201">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; This is</text><text start="1599.309" dur="2.1">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Hello.</text><text start="2129.714" dur="2.1">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Okay.</text><text start="2324.717" dur="2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I</text><text start="2742.721" dur="2.1">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I</text></transcript>